## Original Content
China and India will hold the 25th round of talks between their special representatives on the boundary question in Beijing on Tuesday, the Chinese Foreign Ministry announced on Monday.

## Summary
China and India are set to hold their 25th round of talks on border disputes in Beijing. The meeting aims to address the longstanding boundary question between the two nations. Scheduled for Tuesday, it will be led by their special representatives.

## Key Points
- 25th round of China-India boundary talks to be held in Beijing
- Meeting led by special representatives of both countries
- Primary focus on resolving the boundary question


